{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_hsnacademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by hsnacademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#A_Complete_Video_Solution_with_the_Thought_Process_by_Dr._Xue&#39;s_Math_School\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">A Complete Video Solution with the Thought Process by Dr. Xue's Math School</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many four-digit numbers have all three of the following properties?\n</p><p>(I) The tens and ones digit are both 9.\n</p><p>(II) The number is 1 less than a perfect square.\n</p><p>(III) The number is the product of exactly two prime numbers.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bcd5bbd626bd1e1ecd06b5e602defd55c570b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The \"Condition (II)\" perfect square must end in \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f2c746327924273ba209f0879ea846a0b8dd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$00$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />\" because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba0c606e289b72d611dffc82b28a524c1242a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$...99+1=...00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" /> <i>Condition (I)</i>. Four-digit perfect squares ending in \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f2c746327924273ba209f0879ea846a0b8dd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$00$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />\" are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac9309fdcd78861adf68af01842b1b7fe421437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />, which when squaring these numbers, gets you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/573a687e3c635dfd8a426f93f24cdca469491641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1600, 2500, 3600, 4900, 6400, 8100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" /> respectively.\n</p><p><i>Condition (II)</i> also says the number is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb69df5577de55ff087bfc5fd090a6ea28c5c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. By the <b><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Difference_of_two_squares\">Difference of Squares</a></b>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892d749b594b338b1e3117b6f2cdb04bd1a7dc60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1 = (n+1)(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />. Hence: \n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d700a6987853b4ffd73fd66ec49b6b27fa8fa2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^2-1 = (39)(41)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8c5ffcc232ccd08581d50aaf641173d06d474d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^2-1 = (49)(51)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa7287522ba47c66d109266de481bdf24f44b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^2-1 = (59)(61)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/a/77a207c752d1d629662e874f80a97f2697caab63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^2-1 = (69)(71)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4eaf1bdaf8f0871e9ce326b67029190567c420f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^2-1 = (79)(81)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dfc90f3553432667dc63f32073d52189e45f097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^2-1 = (89)(91)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" /></li></ul>\n<p>On this list, the only number that is the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> prime numbers (condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa7287522ba47c66d109266de481bdf24f44b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^2-1 = (59)(61)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ed2f05435e58fefc7a33879c11c020d9d637cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)\\ 1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"52\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Soupboy0\n</p><p>~ Edited by MICHAEL0926\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=_bBbxic9tr_JdIJJ&amp;t=8427\">https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=_bBbxic9tr_JdIJJ&amp;t=8427</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jTTcscvcQmI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jTTcscvcQmI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_hsnacademy\">Video Solution by hsnacademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by hsnacademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=wexxSYnEz2IcjeIb&amp;t=3539\">https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=wexxSYnEz2IcjeIb&amp;t=3539</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988\">https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jn-qIwv57nQ\">https://youtu.be/jn-qIwv57nQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"A_Complete_Video_Solution_with_the_Thought_Process_by_Dr._Xue.27s_Math_School\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"A_Complete_Video_Solution_with_the_Thought_Process_by_Dr._Xue's_Math_School\">A Complete Video Solution with the Thought Process by Dr. Xue's Math School</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: A Complete Video Solution with the Thought Process by Dr. Xue&#39;s Math School\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aEPPwMIQ52w\">https://youtu.be/aEPPwMIQ52w</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=2350s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=2350s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JvuP6MEUP/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1JvuP6MEUP/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 8\">2025 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/ind